From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 20:05:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 132/138] test(refinery): prove the batch wiring by executing
 each shipped block (gcp-l8td.10)

Nine cases, each extracting a sentinel-delimited block of the shipped formula
through tomllib (any placeholder left over is fatal, except the one case that
leaves {{merge_batch_max}} unrendered on purpose) and running it in a real git
repo against a stub gc and stub merge-batch.sh / merge-push.sh in a staged pack
tree: find-work unrendered, rendered, select-one, routed and truncating; rebase
stack; batch red (serial then the pour block, with no gc call naming a member and
no rejection); merge-push lanes; and the formula/script default drift check,
which is shown to fail when either side of a copy changes.

Red/green: against the base formula every case fails; against one-line mutants
(no BATCH_MAX case, no truncation, no routed guard, no manifest removal on a
failed stack, no drain on a failed serial, -gt 0 for -gt 1, land without --head,
a changed default) exactly the matching case fails. No existing suite is edited.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 gastown/tests/test_refinery_batch_wiring.sh | 514 ++++++++++++++++++++
